                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "Chains as removable chips, + New rack. The library is global to the rig \u2014 racks live beside the device-keyed settings, not inside a session (#442 D1). A session carries references, and a take that inherited a rack carries a frozen copy under the rack\u2019s name: loading a session on another rig must not silently rewrite that rig\u2019s racks, and deleting a rack must not reach into takes that already sound like it. A session bundle embeds the racks it references, so a session moves rigs whole."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
